Detects your stack, logs you in if needed (browser pairing, test-mode
key), installs the matching Reevit SDK, wires REEVIT_* environment variables,
and writes integration starter files — a webhook handler, a checkout
component, or a server-side client, depending on the project.

Existing files are preserved by default. Interactive setup can replace
generated integration files after creating a backup. Checkout can optionally
be inserted into an existing page using an idempotent marked block.

Usage:
  reevit init [flags]

Flags:
      --accessible                  use screen-reader-friendly prompts
      --checkout-fields strings     fields to collect: amount (or price), name, email, phone, reference
      --checkout-metadata strings   custom metadata fields to collect for payments and workflows
      --checkout-page string        existing page where checkout should be added; use - for standalone
      --checkout-path string        custom output path for the checkout component
      --client-path string          custom output path for the server client
      --dry-run                     print what would happen without writing anything
      --fresh                       replace generated integration files and rotate project test credentials
      --goal string                 setup goal: auto, full, checkout, webhook, or server (default "auto")
  -h, --help                        help for init
      --keep-logs                   keep successful setup logs
      --origin string               local checkout origin (defaults to the detected framework port)
      --overwrite                   replace generated integration files after backing them up
      --register-webhook string     register this production webhook endpoint in your dashboard
      --rotate-test-keys            replace project test credentials after local secrets were lost
      --target strings              what to scaffold (webhook, checkout, client) — skips the prompt
      --verbose                     stream package-manager output
      --webhook-path string         custom output path for the webhook handler
  -y, --yes                         scaffold everything available without prompting

Global Flags:
      --no-color   disable colour and glyphs
